WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.200
So you have your why, your purpose, and your where, your vision, now we need your how.

00:07.200 --> 00:09.240
This is your mission.

00:09.240 --> 00:16.360
But before we build it, let's be clear about the risk of operating without an M.V.P. blueprint.

00:16.360 --> 00:22.840
Without it, leaders often feel adrift, making decisions that can lead to burnout, a lack

00:22.840 --> 00:25.540
of focus, and stagnation.

00:25.540 --> 00:28.560
Your blueprint is the antidote.

00:28.560 --> 00:33.860
Your mission is how you activate your purpose and vision every single day.

00:33.860 --> 00:39.680
If your vision is the destination, your mission is a specific vehicle you'll drive, providing

00:39.680 --> 00:42.240
essential clarity and direction.

00:42.240 --> 00:47.440
It's important to know that this mission can and should evolve as you grow.

00:47.440 --> 00:52.520
Think of it as your operational game plan, defining the work you will do to make your

00:52.520 --> 00:54.760
vision a reality.

00:54.760 --> 00:59.560
A powerful mission statement often follows a simple template.

00:59.560 --> 01:10.480
I will action for audience by area of focus to desired result.

01:10.480 --> 01:17.160
For example, I will build for my team by implementing clear systems to create an environment of

01:17.160 --> 01:20.520
clarity and high performance.

01:20.520 --> 01:27.460
Or I will advocate for emerging artists by leveraging my network to secure them galleries

01:27.460 --> 01:28.880
and funding.

01:28.880 --> 01:30.280
It's active.

01:30.280 --> 01:32.060
It's clear.

01:32.060 --> 01:35.200
Your mission acts as a guardrail.

01:35.200 --> 01:40.640
In our busy lives, we're constantly presented with opportunities, requests, and distractions.

01:40.640 --> 01:44.000
A clear mission helps you filter them.

01:44.000 --> 01:50.400
When a new project or opportunity comes up, you can ask, does this align with my mission?

01:50.400 --> 01:57.840
If the answer is no, it's a distraction, and you can say no with confidence.

01:57.840 --> 02:03.320
If yes, it's an opportunity, and you can say yes with conviction.

02:03.320 --> 02:08.600
Head to your playbook to complete the final part of your M.V.P. Blueprint by drafting your

02:08.600 --> 02:10.040
mission statement.

